; The pitch's fall across a sentence. Per segment two cards in (n, send); at a sentence's first frame its summary
; (L and three more, INP at gl); per frame out the pitch so far, 130 - q Hz, q = 30 f / L (f the frame in the
; sentence), at most 30. q moves by Bresenham: each frame adds 30 to qr and takes L away as often as it goes.
;
; Address Contents Label Opcode Operand Comment
  03            seg     INP   i        03-11: a segment (i counts its frames down); after a sentence's end, a new one
  04                    INP   send
  05            frm     CLA   i
  06                    SUB   00
  07                    TAC   eos
  08                    STO   i
  09                    CLA   ns
  10                    SUB   00
  11                    TAC   go
  12            gl      INP   l        12-19: a new sentence: its L
  13            g2      INP   x
  14            g3      INP   x
  15            g4      INP   x
  16                    CLA   z
  17                    STO   q
  18                    STO   qr
  19                    STO   ns
  20            go      CLA   c130     20-44: 130 - q out, q on a frame
  21                    SUB   q
  22                    STO   b
  23                    OUT   b
  24                    CLA   q
  25                    SUB   c30
  26                    TAC   qu
  27                    JMP   frm
  28            qu      CLA   qr
  29                    ADD   c30
  30                    STO   qr
  31            ql      CLA   qr
  32                    SUB   l
  33                    TAC   qd
  34                    STO   qr
  35                    CLA   q
  36                    ADD   00
  37                    STO   q
  38                    JMP   ql
  39            qd      CLA   q
  40                    SUB   c30
  41                    TAC   frm
  42                    CLA   c30
  43                    STO   q
  44                    JMP   frm
  45            eos     CLA   send     45-50: the segment ends a sentence: the next frame starts one
  46                    SUB   00
  47                    TAC   seg
  48                    CLA   00
  49                    STO   ns
  50                    JMP   seg
  60            i       DATA  0
  61            send    DATA  0
  62            ns      DATA  1
  63            l       DATA  0
  64            x       DATA  0
  65            q       DATA  0
  66            qr      DATA  0
  67            b       DATA  0
  68            z       DATA  0
  69            c130    DATA  130
  70            c30     DATA  30
